breachsafe-ux is a deliberate, reviewed Apache-2.0 open-source exception (#19) to the
BreachSAFE platform PolyForm-Noncommercial default, so it can be the public shared
dependency of the open-source QuReddy [ux] extra.


Third-party runtime dependencies
--------------------------------

This product depends at runtime on the following third-party packages, each under its own
license (declared in pyproject.toml [project].dependencies):

  gradio                  Apache License, Version 2.0
  PyYAML                  MIT License
  jsonschema              MIT License
  cyclonedx-python-lib    Apache License, Version 2.0

Each package is distributed by its own authors under the license named above. Those
licenses and copyright notices apply to those packages, not to breachsafe-ux.


Bundled third-party assets
--------------------------

This product bundles the Lucide icon set under src/breachsafe_ux/assets/icons/, which is
Copyright the Lucide Contributors (https://lucide.dev) and licensed under the ISC License.
The icons keep their original ISC license and are not relicensed under Apache-2.0. See the
override annotation for that path in REUSE.toml.


Development-only components (not shipped in the wheel)
-----------------------------------------------------

The canonical BreachSAFE skills installed under .claude/skills/ and .agents/skills/ are
first-party BreachSAFE tooling under the platform PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0 default.
They are development-only agent tooling and are not part of the published wheel, so the
Apache-2.0 grant above does not extend to them. See the annotation for those paths in
REUSE.toml.
